# Pull Request Creation Standards

This file defines mandatory standards for creating Pull Requests in the Spellwright project. All PRs must follow Conventional Commits format for titles and use the structured template for body content.

## PR Creation Triggers

**Activate when user requests:**

- "create a PR", "open a pull request", "create pull request"
- "open PR for SPWT-X" (Task)
- "create PR from current branch"

## Template Loading Strategy

**CRITICAL:** The PR template is loaded **ON-DEMAND**, not automatically in context. You MUST explicitly read the template file when the user requests PR creation.

### When User Requests PR Creation

**Trigger phrases:** "create a PR", "open a pull request", "open PR for SPWT-X"

**Action:**

1. **Read file:** `.cursor/rules/general/pr-template.mdc`
2. Follow the template structure provided in that file
3. Apply all PR Creation Principles from this overview
4. Use Conventional Commits format for title
5. Validate using PR Creation Checklist

## Workflow Overview

1. **Identify Context:**
    - Determine current branch (task branch: `tech/SPWS-X/SPWT-X`, `feature/SPWS-X/SPWT-X`, `bug/SPWS-X/SPWT-X`)
    - Determine target branch (story branch: `feature/develop/SPWS-X`)
    - Fetch task details from Notion if not already in context
    - Get authenticated user info for assignee

2. **Read Template:**
    - Read `.cursor/rules/general/pr-template.mdc`
    - Identify appropriate task-type section (Feature/Tech/Bug)

3. **Generate PR Title:**
    - Follow Conventional Commits format from commit message
    - Use same format as commit: `type(scope): subject`
    - Examples: `feat(components): implement core spell components`, `fix(collision): prevent null reference`

4. **Analyze and Assign Labels:**
    - **Automatically assign labels** based on PR content and task information
    - See "Automatic Label Assignment" section below for rules
    - Apply 3-5 labels per PR (type, priority, area/spell/dots, optional status)

5. **Generate PR Body:**
    - Follow template structure from `pr-template.mdc`
    - Remove INSTRUCTION/FORMAT/EXAMPLE labels
    - Populate with task-specific information
    - Include only relevant task-type section

6. **Create PR:**
    - Use GitHub MCP `create_pull_request` tool
    - Set `draft: false` (unless explicitly requested as draft)
    - Verify PR created successfully

7. **Assign to Creator:**
    - Use GitHub MCP `update_pull_request` to assign PR to creator
    - Get creator username from `mcp_github_get_me` if needed
    - Assignee = person responsible for the PR (always the creator)

8. **Apply Labels:**
    - Use GitHub CLI or API to add automatically determined labels
    - Apply all labels in a single operation if possible

9. **Update Notion:**
    - Use `notion-update-page` to set Pull Request property with PR URL
    - Confirm update successful

## Automatic Label Assignment

**CRITICAL:** Labels MUST be automatically assigned based on PR content and task information. The agent MUST analyze the PR and determine appropriate labels without asking the user.

### Label Assignment Rules

Apply **3-5 labels minimum** to every PR, following this structure:

1. **1x Type Label** (MANDATORY)
2. **1x Priority Label** (MANDATORY)
3. **1-2x Context Labels** (area/spell/dots) (MANDATORY)
4. **0-2x Additional Labels** (status/performance/etc) (OPTIONAL)

### Type Label (MANDATORY - Choose ONE)

Based on **branch type** or **commit type**:

| Branch/Commit Pattern        | Label            | When to Use                              |
| ---------------------------- | ---------------- | ---------------------------------------- |
| `feature/` or `feat:`        | `type: feature`  | New functionality, components, systems   |
| `bug/` or `fix:`             | `type: bug`      | Bug fixes, error corrections             |
| `tech/` or `refactor:`       | `type: tech`     | Refactoring, tech debt, code cleanup     |
| `docs:`                      | `type: docs`     | Documentation only changes               |
| `test:`                      | `type: test`     | Test-related changes                     |
| `.github/workflows/` changes | `type: ci/cd`    | CI/CD, workflows, rulesets               |
| Breaking API changes         | `type: breaking` | Incompatible changes (add to other type) |

### Priority Label (MANDATORY - Choose ONE)

Based on **Notion task Priority** or **urgency**:

| Notion Priority | Label                | When to Use                              |
| --------------- | -------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |
| High/Critical   | `priority: critical` | Blockers, critical bugs, security issues |
| High            | `priority: high`     | Important features, high-impact bugs     |
| Medium          | `priority: medium`   | Normal features, moderate bugs           |
| Low             | `priority: low`      | Nice-to-have, minor improvements         |

**Default:** If priority not specified in Notion, use `priority: medium`

### Context Labels (MANDATORY - Choose 1-2)

#### Spell System Labels

Use when PR affects **spell-specific functionality**:

| Label              | When to Use               | Keywords to Look For                                                     |
| ------------------ | ------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| `spell: generator` | Generators implementation | "Projectile", "Cone", "AoE", "Self-Cast", "spawn", "instantiate"         |
| `spell: modifier`  | Modifiers implementation  | "Homing", "Chain", "Pierce", "Fork", "Split", "Bounce"                   |
| `spell: payload`   | Payloads implementation   | "Damage", "Heal", "Status", "Effect", "DOT", "Buff", "Debuff"            |
| `spell: component` | Spell components          | "Velocity", "Lifetime", "SpellOwner", "Target", spell-related components |

#### DOTS/ECS Labels

Use when PR affects **Unity DOTS/ECS architecture**:

| Label             | When to Use            | Keywords to Look For                                              |
| ----------------- | ---------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `dots: system`    | Systems implementation | "ISystem", "SystemBase", "OnUpdate", "OnCreate", system logic     |
| `dots: component` | Components             | "IComponentData", "IBufferElementData", "IEnableableComponent"    |
| `dots: job`       | Jobs                   | "IJobEntity", "IJobChunk", "IJobParallelFor", Burst jobs          |
| `dots: burst`     | Burst optimization     | "Burst", "[BurstCompile]", optimization, SIMD                     |
| `dots: entities`  | Entity management      | "EntityManager", "EntityQuery", "EntityCommandBuffer", archetypes |

#### Area Labels

Use when PR affects **specific game system area**:

| Label                | When to Use          | Keywords to Look For                                             |
| -------------------- | -------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `area: architecture` | Architecture changes | "architecture", "design pattern", "structure", major refactoring |
| `area: input`        | Input system         | "Input System", "InputAction", "PlayerInput", controls           |
| `area: physics`      | Physics              | "Physics", "collision", "trigger", "raycast", "overlap"          |
| `area: rendering`    | Rendering/Graphics   | "rendering", "shader", "material", "VFX", "particle"             |
| `area: networking`   | Networking           | "NetCode", "multiplayer", "RPC", "synchronization"               |
| `area: ui`           | User Interface       | "UI", "Canvas", "Button", "UIToolkit", menu                      |
| `area: audio`        | Audio                | "audio", "sound", "music", "AudioSource", "AudioClip"            |

### Additional Labels (OPTIONAL - Choose 0-2)

#### Status Labels

| Label                   | When to Use                            |
| ----------------------- | -------------------------------------- |
| `status: blocked`       | PR depends on another PR/issue         |
| `status: needs design`  | Requires architecture discussion       |
| `status: needs testing` | Implementation done, waiting for tests |

#### Performance Labels

| Label            | When to Use                                     |
| ---------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |
| `quick win`      | Easy to implement, high impact (< 2 hours work) |
| `performance`    | Optimization, performance improvements          |
| `technical debt` | Addresses tech debt                             |

#### Special Labels

| Label              | When to Use                                               |
| ------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------- |
| `skip-title-check` | PR title doesn't follow Conventional Commits (use RARELY) |

